{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Hearken to Me, My people.</b> These are the words of HaShem." "<b>A teaching shall go forth from Me.</b> It is prophecy." "<b>I will cause to rest.</b> Like אניח, and like it זאת המרגעה (Isaiah 28:12). And one of the commentators said that ארגיע means 'I will do in a moment without delay,' but the first interpretation is correct."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:55.612593857Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}